[Music]  rarely do nature and architecture come  together so perfectly as a divine Greek  monasteries of meteora meteor is a  collection of Greek Orthodox monasteries  perched on rock pillars 1,300 feet above  ground they are built by Greek monks  from the 14th and 16th centuries they  were constructed by using a network of  ropes pulleys baskets and ladders which  lifted supplies up the dramatic cliffs  in a vision to solitude the location  brought the monks and locals a place of  protection from unwanted trespassers and  a sanctuary during invasions from the  Turks today only six of the original 20  monasteries remains but they are still  inhabited by 20 monks and four nuns who  are full-time residents the meteora is  one of only a handful of places that are  listed as a unesco world heritage site  under two categories nature and art  without changing the landscape the monks  managed to build monasteries that seemed  like extensions of the mountain itself  the day meteoric translates to suspended  in space these monasteries truly seem to  defy gravity  [Music]  you  [Music]

